1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:45,928
I knew this would happen, but after I became a second-year student, Mr. Hayashida was no longer my teacher.

2
00:01:50,808 --> 00:01:52,688
I guess it's lunchtime now.

3
00:01:52,708 --> 00:01:55,848
Hurry up! Before they sell out the double hamburgers and lunch sandwiches!

4
00:01:55,868 --> 00:01:58,408
Well, I'm getting the fried chicken potato salad sandwich!

5
00:01:58,908 --> 00:01:59,948
Ball is your friend!

6
00:01:59,948 --> 00:02:01,148
I'm coming for you, world!

7
00:02:01,508 --> 00:02:06,188
Hey, is it true he's a year older?

8
00:02:06,408 --> 00:02:09,228
Then that means he's repeating the year, but I wonder why?

9
00:02:09,388 --> 00:02:11,808
I heard that. He's really into shogi.

10
00:02:12,028 --> 00:02:14,068
Is it shogi a game for old men?

11
00:02:14,428 --> 00:02:15,708
A game played at home?

12
00:02:15,968 --> 00:02:17,068
Is he an otaku?

13
00:02:17,408 --> 00:02:19,808
Is he repeating because he ditched so much school?

14
00:02:20,188 --> 00:02:21,368
Hmm, probably.

15
00:02:22,288 --> 00:02:24,608
I... I gotta get out of here.

16
00:02:24,608 --> 00:02:34,108
When the new school term started, everyone in my class immediately formed into groups.

17
00:02:34,908 --> 00:02:38,488
They splintered off into little cliques and pretty much just kept to themselves.

18
00:02:38,488 --> 00:02:43,628
So how is a loser like me with no courage or friends supposed to join any of them?

19
00:02:43,628 --> 00:02:47,048
Hey, mind if I sit with you?

20
00:02:48,528 --> 00:02:49,528
Was that weird?

21
00:02:50,208 --> 00:02:52,368
Oh, no. More normal and less eager.

22
00:02:53,188 --> 00:02:55,528
Hey, would it be okay if I ate with you?

23
00:02:55,528 --> 00:02:59,028
Just like that. Nice and smooth.

24
00:02:59,528 --> 00:03:04,068
As if I could do that, then I wouldn't be eating lunch by myself for 11 years!

25
00:03:04,748 --> 00:03:06,348
Nope. It's impossible.

26
00:03:06,908 --> 00:03:09,088
I'd definitely stumble like a dork.

27
00:03:09,088 --> 00:03:15,868
Well, this is pretty much what I expected.

28
00:03:16,648 --> 00:03:18,868
I'm just gonna have to bear it alone quietly.

29
00:03:19,848 --> 00:03:20,868
Two more years.

30
00:03:21,448 --> 00:03:23,208
Just two more years of being alone.

31
00:03:23,768 --> 00:03:27,028
More importantly, the rank-deciding competition starts in June,

32
00:03:27,468 --> 00:03:30,168
and I need to focus on my matches in the rookie tournament.

33
00:03:30,728 --> 00:03:32,328
The rank-deciding competition.

34
00:03:33,068 --> 00:03:35,628
There are 34 C1 players in my class.

35
00:03:35,628 --> 00:03:41,008
Ten matches are arranged by lottery for those 34 players to participate in.

36
00:03:41,808 --> 00:03:44,368
Only the top two players will be promoted to B2.

37
00:03:45,188 --> 00:03:47,948
But Nikaida wasn't listed on the match schedule anywhere.

38
00:03:49,388 --> 00:03:50,908
Kiriyama, what is this?

39
00:03:51,228 --> 00:03:52,188
How should I know?

40
00:03:52,348 --> 00:03:53,508
Are you at the Shogi Hall?

41
00:03:53,668 --> 00:03:54,988
Wait for me, I'm on my way!

42
00:03:57,248 --> 00:04:00,288
Now you and I are gonna have to go for it in the rookie tournament.

43
00:04:01,648 --> 00:04:04,608
It's too bad that we're in completely separate blocks.

44
00:04:04,608 --> 00:04:08,488
But, we'll just have to keep winning so we can meet in the finals!

45
00:04:08,828 --> 00:04:09,528
Hey, wait!

46
00:04:09,628 --> 00:04:11,228
What do you mean we'll meet in the finals?

47
00:04:11,528 --> 00:04:12,528
Give me a break!

48
00:04:12,628 --> 00:04:14,648
You can't make snap decisions like that!

49
00:04:15,028 --> 00:04:15,888
Why not?

50
00:04:15,948 --> 00:04:17,068
It's the truth, isn't it?

51
00:04:17,128 --> 00:04:18,228
Now don't falter!

52
00:04:20,128 --> 00:04:20,548
Hmm.

53
00:04:21,088 --> 00:04:22,988
The legend between us...

54
00:04:22,988 --> 00:04:26,388
has only just begun, trust me.

55
00:04:26,748 --> 00:04:27,708
Legend?

56
00:04:27,708 --> 00:04:28,708
Legend?

57
00:04:28,708 --> 00:04:30,808
And why is it ours?

58
00:04:31,708 --> 00:04:33,288
Uh, yeah, sure.

59
00:04:33,868 --> 00:04:35,888
Looking forward to it.

60
00:04:39,168 --> 00:04:41,428
Yeah, I'll have to do my best.

61
00:04:42,008 --> 00:04:43,528
Because that's all I can do.

62
00:04:44,188 --> 00:04:45,708
For both the rookie tournament,

63
00:04:46,288 --> 00:04:47,968
and the rank-deciding competition.

64
00:04:47,968 --> 00:04:50,848
That's what I heard.

65
00:04:50,848 --> 00:04:50,908
That's what I heard.

66
00:04:50,908 --> 00:04:51,348
I think so.

67
00:04:54,228 --> 00:04:54,788
Yeah.

68
00:05:04,268 --> 00:05:05,568
I'll do my best.

69
00:05:06,108 --> 00:05:07,388
One move at a time again.

70
00:05:07,728 --> 00:05:08,628
Right from the start.

71
00:05:10,088 --> 00:05:11,788
One move at a time.

72
00:05:11,788 --> 00:05:14,408
Hey, Kiriyama!

73
00:05:15,248 --> 00:05:16,828
Hold it right there!

74
00:05:23,908 --> 00:05:25,408
Damn you, Kiriyama!

75
00:05:26,108 --> 00:05:27,188
Mr. Hayashida?

76
00:05:27,488 --> 00:05:28,808
What are you doing?

77
00:05:29,048 --> 00:05:31,288
You shouldn't just abandon the students you were with.

78
00:05:32,248 --> 00:05:34,308
I don't give a crap about that!

79
00:05:34,628 --> 00:05:37,168
What am I supposed to do when I see a student look like that?

80
00:05:37,348 --> 00:05:38,888
I have to run to his rescue!

81
00:05:39,928 --> 00:05:41,608
You got it!

82
00:05:42,108 --> 00:05:43,768
A student look like what?

83
00:05:44,068 --> 00:05:45,328
I don't get it.

84
00:05:46,188 --> 00:05:46,928
Come here!

85
00:05:46,968 --> 00:05:48,288
It's written all over your face!

86
00:05:48,348 --> 00:05:49,208
Are you kidding?!

87
00:05:54,848 --> 00:05:56,328
So, um...

88
00:05:56,328 --> 00:05:56,648
Yeah?

89
00:05:56,908 --> 00:05:57,268
What?

90
00:05:57,588 --> 00:05:58,648
So, is it...

91
00:05:58,648 --> 00:06:01,768
all right for you to have lunch with me,

92
00:06:01,868 --> 00:06:03,528
even though you're not my teacher this year?

93
00:06:04,028 --> 00:06:05,088
Oh, yeah, sure.

94
00:06:05,568 --> 00:06:07,908
I just saw my former introverted student

95
00:06:07,908 --> 00:06:09,628
who barely passed the attendance requirement

96
00:06:09,628 --> 00:06:11,188
due to certain circumstances

97
00:06:11,188 --> 00:06:12,148
looking depressed.

98
00:06:12,608 --> 00:06:13,508
When I told them,

99
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:14,448
the class said,

100
00:06:14,568 --> 00:06:15,448
Mr. Hayashida,

101
00:06:15,548 --> 00:06:16,648
you gotta help him!

102
00:06:16,768 --> 00:06:17,988
Wait a minute, no fair.

103
00:06:18,108 --> 00:06:19,928
Why are you making me sound like a big loser

104
00:06:19,928 --> 00:06:21,668
while you get to be some kind of hero?

105
00:06:21,908 --> 00:06:23,088
Because I want to be invited

106
00:06:23,088 --> 00:06:25,008
to the students' Christmas party this year.

107
00:06:25,348 --> 00:06:27,248
I've been feeling a little depressed, too.

108
00:06:27,248 --> 00:06:29,928
But still,

109
00:06:30,568 --> 00:06:32,508
why did you come back here,

110
00:06:32,628 --> 00:06:33,168
Kiriyama?

111
00:06:34,308 --> 00:06:35,468
It's a new year

112
00:06:35,468 --> 00:06:36,628
and a new school term.

113
00:06:36,948 --> 00:06:38,128
This is your last chance.

114
00:06:38,568 --> 00:06:39,968
If you don't apply yourself now,

115
00:06:40,028 --> 00:06:40,928
then when will you?

116
00:06:40,928 --> 00:06:46,868
You are making an effort, right?

117
00:06:47,908 --> 00:06:48,948
I sure hope so.

118
00:06:49,388 --> 00:06:51,028
I can't encourage you to do your best

119
00:06:51,028 --> 00:06:51,948
any more than that.

120
00:06:53,628 --> 00:06:54,148
So,

121
00:06:54,528 --> 00:06:56,028
I have a great idea.

122
00:06:59,608 --> 00:07:01,288
Let's make our own Shogi Club.

123
00:07:01,288 --> 00:07:07,928
Our own Shogi Club?

124
00:07:09,568 --> 00:07:09,868
Huh?

125
00:07:10,188 --> 00:07:10,788
But wait.

126
00:07:11,548 --> 00:07:12,968
I'll be the faculty advisor.

127
00:07:13,848 --> 00:07:14,388
If so,

128
00:07:14,488 --> 00:07:15,428
then it wouldn't be strange

129
00:07:15,428 --> 00:07:16,488
for me to look after you.

130
00:07:16,788 --> 00:07:17,668
I'd be your advisor.

131
00:07:18,748 --> 00:07:21,088
But that sounds easier said than done.

132
00:07:21,428 --> 00:07:22,368
Just five members

133
00:07:22,368 --> 00:07:24,148
and a faculty advisor makes a club.

134
00:07:24,328 --> 00:07:25,328
Yeah, but still.

135
00:07:25,708 --> 00:07:27,348
All we need are four more members.

136
00:07:27,668 --> 00:07:28,968
But I don't know anyone

137
00:07:28,968 --> 00:07:30,308
who would be interested.

138
00:07:30,528 --> 00:07:32,228
Let's just look into it and see.

139
00:07:32,488 --> 00:07:32,928
Okay.

140
00:07:33,228 --> 00:07:35,088
But I doubt that'll be very easy to do.

141
00:07:36,008 --> 00:07:38,568
You sound like a broken record.

142
00:07:38,888 --> 00:07:39,568
Not at all.

143
00:07:39,788 --> 00:07:40,788
It's nothing like that.

144
00:07:43,008 --> 00:07:44,128
Ah, Kiriyama.

145
00:07:44,868 --> 00:07:47,068
Why do you think you took another shot

146
00:07:47,068 --> 00:07:48,908
at being a high school student this year?

147
00:07:49,808 --> 00:07:50,508
Was it to

148
00:07:50,508 --> 00:07:52,068
eat lunch all alone

149
00:07:52,068 --> 00:07:53,648
sitting on the stairs like this?

150
00:07:55,228 --> 00:07:56,568
Of course not.

151
00:07:57,088 --> 00:07:57,408
Right?

152
00:07:58,968 --> 00:08:05,148
Will this make it seem like

153
00:08:05,148 --> 00:08:06,088
I'm not running away?

154
00:08:07,088 --> 00:08:08,628
What if I'm only pretending

155
00:08:08,628 --> 00:08:09,648
not to run away?

156
00:08:13,128 --> 00:08:14,468
The truth is

157
00:08:14,468 --> 00:08:18,888
it's always weighed heavily on me.

158
00:08:21,128 --> 00:08:22,668
And I knew it too.

159
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:26,868
At this rate

160
00:08:26,868 --> 00:08:28,408
things would only become

161
00:08:28,408 --> 00:08:29,628
more painful for me.

162
00:08:31,488 --> 00:08:33,148
I remember when it hit me.

163
00:08:33,788 --> 00:08:34,588
I kept thinking

164
00:08:34,588 --> 00:08:37,108
if only I could blend in better.

165
00:08:38,008 --> 00:08:38,748
I wish.

166
00:08:39,608 --> 00:08:40,528
Just imagine.

167
00:08:43,208 --> 00:08:45,268
Imagine how happy I could be.

168
00:08:45,268 --> 00:08:50,388
Mr. Hayashida.

169
00:08:50,388 --> 00:08:52,328
Would you please be

170
00:08:52,328 --> 00:08:53,808
the club's advisor?

171
00:08:54,648 --> 00:08:55,388
Of course.

172
00:08:56,688 --> 00:08:57,668
Oh, and Kiriyama.

173
00:08:58,068 --> 00:08:59,028
I hope you know that

174
00:08:59,028 --> 00:09:00,928
you'll be coaching me too.

175
00:09:01,308 --> 00:09:01,568
Right?

176
00:09:02,548 --> 00:09:02,848
Oh.

177
00:09:03,268 --> 00:09:03,768
Okay.

178
00:09:04,268 --> 00:09:04,788
All right.

179
00:09:05,008 --> 00:09:05,648
There it is.

180
00:09:05,808 --> 00:09:07,148
Free professional advice.

181
00:09:07,388 --> 00:09:07,768
Great.

182
00:09:08,088 --> 00:09:08,308
See?

183
00:09:08,508 --> 00:09:09,508
I want to get beyond the wall

184
00:09:09,508 --> 00:09:10,368
and I'm a fourth den.

185
00:09:10,648 --> 00:09:11,488
There's this jerk

186
00:09:11,488 --> 00:09:12,848
that I really want to beat on.

187
00:09:13,128 --> 00:09:13,988
Net Shogi 24.

188
00:09:14,348 --> 00:09:15,288
I'm confused.

189
00:09:15,748 --> 00:09:16,608
Just a minute ago

190
00:09:16,608 --> 00:09:18,388
I was moved by your kindness.

191
00:09:18,388 --> 00:09:25,788
Nobody wants to join.

192
00:09:26,108 --> 00:09:26,848
But why?

193
00:09:27,088 --> 00:09:28,628
Is Shogi really that dull?

194
00:09:29,748 --> 00:09:30,628
Everyone's like,

195
00:09:30,748 --> 00:09:32,668
Shogi, sorry, I'm not interested.

196
00:09:33,048 --> 00:09:34,268
What's up with that?

197
00:09:34,468 --> 00:09:36,548
And I love it so much.

198
00:09:37,028 --> 00:09:37,988
I'm sorry, sir.

199
00:09:38,328 --> 00:09:40,368
There's no reason for you to apologize.

200
00:09:41,028 --> 00:09:42,468
I kind of feel responsible.

201
00:09:42,908 --> 00:09:43,828
That's it!

202
00:09:45,748 --> 00:09:46,348
Noguchi!

203
00:09:48,388 --> 00:09:49,108
Wow!

204
00:09:49,908 --> 00:09:51,408
It stinks in here again!

205
00:09:51,508 --> 00:09:52,488
Hello, Mr. Hayashida.

206
00:09:52,648 --> 00:09:53,628
Long time no see.

207
00:09:54,308 --> 00:09:56,148
What are you guys doing this time?

208
00:09:57,588 --> 00:09:58,568
As you can see,

209
00:09:58,688 --> 00:09:59,968
we're harvesting natto.

210
00:10:00,748 --> 00:10:01,988
Okay, that's odd,

211
00:10:02,088 --> 00:10:03,748
but why make natto here at school?

212
00:10:03,848 --> 00:10:04,428
Well, you see,

213
00:10:04,548 --> 00:10:05,868
we wrapped steamed soybeans

214
00:10:05,868 --> 00:10:06,628
in rice straw

215
00:10:06,628 --> 00:10:07,568
and keep them warm

216
00:10:07,568 --> 00:10:09,488
at 100 degrees Fahrenheit overnight.

217
00:10:09,868 --> 00:10:10,988
That allows the bacillus

218
00:10:10,988 --> 00:10:12,328
to subtilize in the straw

219
00:10:12,328 --> 00:10:13,868
and spread to the soybeans,

220
00:10:14,008 --> 00:10:15,408
which proliferates fermentation.

221
00:10:16,168 --> 00:10:16,648
Okay.

222
00:10:16,648 --> 00:10:18,708
Well, I wasn't really asking you guys

223
00:10:18,708 --> 00:10:19,968
about how you made it.

224
00:10:20,188 --> 00:10:20,668
Wow!

225
00:10:20,948 --> 00:10:22,868
Yup, this is the real deal.

226
00:10:23,088 --> 00:10:24,928
You're eating that already?

227
00:10:25,808 --> 00:10:27,908
Sometimes you can be surprisingly random.

228
00:10:28,908 --> 00:10:29,388
Anyway,

229
00:10:29,568 --> 00:10:30,408
how were you guys able

230
00:10:30,408 --> 00:10:31,528
to find the rice straw?

231
00:10:31,928 --> 00:10:34,308
I thought you'd never ask.

232
00:10:34,488 --> 00:10:36,388
This is what I did for my thesis.

233
00:10:36,748 --> 00:10:38,108
I grew a plot of rice

234
00:10:38,108 --> 00:10:39,588
on the school roof last year

235
00:10:39,588 --> 00:10:41,388
and then harvested the straw.

236
00:10:41,388 --> 00:10:42,428
Wait a second.

237
00:10:42,788 --> 00:10:43,888
What kind of thesis?

238
00:10:44,168 --> 00:10:45,768
Who exactly are you presenting it to

239
00:10:45,768 --> 00:10:47,088
and what is it even for?

240
00:10:47,328 --> 00:10:48,088
And come on,

241
00:10:48,148 --> 00:10:49,608
you know that's not allowed at school.

242
00:10:50,388 --> 00:10:52,788
The entire concept is ridiculous.

243
00:10:53,348 --> 00:10:53,888
Oh, wait!

244
00:10:54,068 --> 00:10:55,648
I almost forgot why I'm here.

245
00:10:55,828 --> 00:10:56,528
That's right!

246
00:10:56,908 --> 00:10:57,388
Noguchi,

247
00:10:57,528 --> 00:10:58,868
do you know how to play Shogi?

248
00:10:59,728 --> 00:11:00,128
Shogi?

249
00:11:00,128 --> 00:11:02,568
Well, my grandfather taught me

250
00:11:02,568 --> 00:11:03,988
to play it when I was a kid.

251
00:11:04,448 --> 00:11:06,888
And it's a rather intense game,

252
00:11:06,968 --> 00:11:07,488
isn't it?

253
00:11:08,388 --> 00:11:09,228
It is!

254
00:11:09,408 --> 00:11:10,468
So here's the deal.

255
00:11:10,568 --> 00:11:11,648
We're trying to put together

256
00:11:11,648 --> 00:11:12,508
a Shogi club,

257
00:11:12,668 --> 00:11:14,208
but we need four more members.

258
00:11:14,568 --> 00:11:16,008
And now we finally got one!

259
00:11:16,828 --> 00:11:18,668
Sounds like we're in the same boat.

260
00:11:19,128 --> 00:11:20,348
The future of my

261
00:11:20,348 --> 00:11:21,668
after-school burners club

262
00:11:21,668 --> 00:11:22,388
is in peril.

263
00:11:23,088 --> 00:11:24,768
The club could even be disbanded

264
00:11:24,768 --> 00:11:25,868
at the next budget meeting

265
00:11:25,868 --> 00:11:26,868
coming up in May.

266
00:11:27,628 --> 00:11:28,108
What?

267
00:11:28,368 --> 00:11:30,488
But I thought you had lots of members.

268
00:11:30,668 --> 00:11:31,328
So what happened?

269
00:11:32,368 --> 00:11:35,128
All of the upperclassmen

270
00:11:35,128 --> 00:11:36,928
have graduated and moved on.

271
00:11:38,708 --> 00:11:39,568
Wait a minute.

272
00:11:39,888 --> 00:11:41,728
Those members were older than you?

273
00:11:43,128 --> 00:11:43,688
Hello!

274
00:11:43,908 --> 00:11:45,008
Is this the science club?

275
00:11:45,308 --> 00:11:45,828
Teacher?

276
00:11:46,268 --> 00:11:47,528
No, club president!

277
00:11:48,188 --> 00:11:50,228
Yes, they were marvelous mentors.

278
00:11:50,728 --> 00:11:52,048
From the day I joined the club,

279
00:11:52,048 --> 00:11:52,888
even though I was

280
00:11:52,888 --> 00:11:53,908
a first-year student,

281
00:11:54,088 --> 00:11:55,308
they called me teacher.

282
00:11:57,628 --> 00:11:59,288
I want to keep the club going

283
00:11:59,288 --> 00:12:00,388
and have the opportunity

284
00:12:00,388 --> 00:12:02,008
to pass the wonders of science

285
00:12:02,008 --> 00:12:03,468
on to younger students.

286
00:12:04,128 --> 00:12:06,048
But with only four members left,

287
00:12:06,108 --> 00:12:07,388
it'll be the end of us.

288
00:12:07,628 --> 00:12:08,388
No more.

289
00:12:08,568 --> 00:12:10,488
If only I could complete my thesis.

290
00:12:10,968 --> 00:12:11,748
Even if you did,

291
00:12:11,808 --> 00:12:13,148
I highly doubt it'll pass on

292
00:12:13,148 --> 00:12:14,348
the joys of science.

293
00:12:17,048 --> 00:12:19,068
Hey, wait a minute!

294
00:12:19,988 --> 00:12:20,688
I've got it!

295
00:12:20,788 --> 00:12:21,848
We can join clubs!

296
00:12:22,348 --> 00:12:23,288
Combine with us

297
00:12:23,288 --> 00:12:23,948
and we'll create

298
00:12:23,948 --> 00:12:25,168
a brand new club together!

299
00:12:32,508 --> 00:12:32,988
Yes!

300
00:12:33,528 --> 00:12:34,708
That makes sense!

301
00:12:36,708 --> 00:12:37,528
All right!

302
00:12:37,708 --> 00:12:39,128
And without further ado,

303
00:12:39,308 --> 00:12:40,388
let's play a game!

304
00:12:40,588 --> 00:12:42,028
I've been kind of holding back,

305
00:12:42,128 --> 00:12:43,388
but now I can play

306
00:12:43,388 --> 00:12:44,288
all the matches I want

307
00:12:44,288 --> 00:12:44,928
with Kiriyama!

308
00:12:44,928 --> 00:12:46,828
Since I'm the faculty advisor!

309
00:12:47,128 --> 00:12:47,328
Ha!

310
00:12:47,468 --> 00:12:48,068
Lucky me!

311
00:12:48,528 --> 00:12:49,008
Noguchi,

312
00:12:49,308 --> 00:12:50,028
I'm sorry.

313
00:12:50,588 --> 00:12:51,728
Are you okay with this?

314
00:12:52,088 --> 00:12:53,328
I feel like I'm imposing

315
00:12:53,328 --> 00:12:54,088
on you again.

316
00:12:54,348 --> 00:12:55,928
I'm actually kind of excited

317
00:12:55,928 --> 00:12:56,508
about it.

318
00:12:57,008 --> 00:12:58,088
After my grandfather

319
00:12:58,088 --> 00:12:58,748
passed away,

320
00:12:58,888 --> 00:13:00,088
I wasn't able to find

321
00:13:00,088 --> 00:13:01,148
anyone to play with.

322
00:13:03,208 --> 00:13:04,828
I'm still just a novice,

323
00:13:05,008 --> 00:13:06,108
but I'd be honored

324
00:13:06,108 --> 00:13:07,308
if you'd teach me too,

325
00:13:07,308 --> 00:13:08,228
Kiriyama.

326
00:13:08,228 --> 00:13:12,248
Yes, of course.

327
00:13:13,408 --> 00:13:14,848
I'd be happy to.

328
00:13:18,848 --> 00:13:19,508
And so,

329
00:13:19,888 --> 00:13:21,188
the Afterschool Burners Club

330
00:13:21,188 --> 00:13:21,628
became

331
00:13:21,628 --> 00:13:23,948
the Afterschool Shogi Science Club.

332
00:13:24,848 --> 00:13:25,728
This is how

333
00:13:25,728 --> 00:13:26,968
my second year started.

334
00:13:28,448 --> 00:13:29,408
A club.

335
00:13:30,048 --> 00:13:31,128
A new club, huh?

336
00:13:31,588 --> 00:13:32,968
And a shogi club at that.

337
00:13:33,628 --> 00:13:34,108
Whoa.

338
00:13:36,028 --> 00:13:36,588
See?

339
00:13:36,768 --> 00:13:37,628
Just like I said.

340
00:13:38,768 --> 00:13:39,868
After we left,

341
00:13:40,128 --> 00:13:41,228
Mr. Hayashita said,

342
00:13:41,888 --> 00:13:42,828
I find it easier

343
00:13:42,828 --> 00:13:43,828
to do something

344
00:13:43,828 --> 00:13:45,588
than just worry about it.

345
00:13:45,988 --> 00:13:47,128
At least 80%

346
00:13:47,128 --> 00:13:48,208
of the time it is.

347
00:13:49,248 --> 00:13:50,388
His enthusiasm

348
00:13:50,388 --> 00:13:51,868
gave me confidence.

349
00:14:04,768 --> 00:14:06,248
The seat next to me

350
00:14:06,248 --> 00:14:07,468
is always empty.

351
00:14:11,048 --> 00:14:11,568
What?

352
00:14:11,628 --> 00:14:13,168
I have to sit next to Kiriyama?

353
00:14:13,428 --> 00:14:15,008
No way I'm doing that.

354
00:14:16,588 --> 00:14:17,148
Teacher,

355
00:14:17,428 --> 00:14:17,988
excuse me.

356
00:14:18,128 --> 00:14:18,868
I have a question.

357
00:14:19,388 --> 00:14:20,268
Can I change seats

358
00:14:20,268 --> 00:14:21,368
and sit somewhere else?

359
00:14:21,828 --> 00:14:22,888
Knock it off, Kaneda.

360
00:14:23,108 --> 00:14:23,848
Just sit down.

361
00:14:23,868 --> 00:14:24,528
Oh, come on,

362
00:14:24,568 --> 00:14:25,328
teacher, please.

363
00:14:25,648 --> 00:14:26,728
You heard what he said.

364
00:14:26,848 --> 00:14:27,968
Hurry up and sit down.

365
00:14:28,008 --> 00:14:29,248
There's lots of other seats.

366
00:14:29,448 --> 00:14:30,028
You don't mind

367
00:14:30,028 --> 00:14:30,908
if I move, right?

368
00:14:31,028 --> 00:14:32,508
Fine, then please hurry up.

369
00:14:32,748 --> 00:14:33,188
Yes!

370
00:14:34,848 --> 00:14:35,908
Okay, everyone.

371
00:14:36,128 --> 00:14:37,088
The class is leaving.

372
00:14:37,668 --> 00:14:39,228
Hey, sit down right now.

373
00:14:39,468 --> 00:14:40,648
At times like this,

374
00:14:40,688 --> 00:14:41,728
I always feel like

375
00:14:41,728 --> 00:14:43,168
if you don't want

376
00:14:43,168 --> 00:14:43,988
to sit by me,

377
00:14:44,108 --> 00:14:44,868
that's fine.

378
00:14:45,668 --> 00:14:47,728
But you don't have to be so loud

379
00:14:47,728 --> 00:14:48,808
and cause a scene

380
00:14:48,808 --> 00:14:49,788
in front of everyone.

381
00:14:49,928 --> 00:14:50,228
I know,

382
00:14:50,308 --> 00:14:51,188
he's really loud.

383
00:14:53,128 --> 00:14:54,368
But once the bus

384
00:14:54,368 --> 00:14:55,108
started moving,

385
00:14:55,708 --> 00:14:56,808
I began to feel

386
00:14:56,808 --> 00:14:58,488
a little bit better.

387
00:15:00,088 --> 00:15:00,948
After all,

388
00:15:01,328 --> 00:15:03,028
it's much easier

389
00:15:03,028 --> 00:15:04,788
to be left all alone

390
00:15:04,788 --> 00:15:06,568
than it is to be forced

391
00:15:06,568 --> 00:15:07,848
to sit next to someone

392
00:15:07,848 --> 00:15:09,068
who hates you.

393
00:15:09,068 --> 00:15:17,728
All right, everyone.

394
00:15:17,868 --> 00:15:19,048
It's time for lunch now.

395
00:15:19,428 --> 00:15:20,188
After lunch,

396
00:15:20,268 --> 00:15:20,928
use the restroom

397
00:15:20,928 --> 00:15:22,008
and be back at the bus

398
00:15:22,008 --> 00:15:22,808
by 1.30.

399
00:15:23,088 --> 00:15:23,528
Okay.

400
00:15:24,528 --> 00:15:25,008
Good.

401
00:15:25,208 --> 00:15:26,688
Be back in an hour and a half.

402
00:15:27,368 --> 00:15:27,928
Dismissed.

403
00:15:35,508 --> 00:15:36,388
Oh, no.

404
00:15:36,388 --> 00:15:38,468
What am I supposed

405
00:15:38,468 --> 00:15:39,328
to do here?

406
00:15:41,208 --> 00:15:42,848
The field is huge.

407
00:15:43,168 --> 00:15:45,108
There's no escape zone anywhere.

408
00:15:47,348 --> 00:15:48,948
Eating my lunch all alone

409
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:50,788
in a wide open field like this,

410
00:15:50,948 --> 00:15:53,188
there's nowhere for me to hide.

411
00:15:53,708 --> 00:15:54,528
And if the teacher

412
00:15:54,528 --> 00:15:56,388
finds me all alone...

413
00:15:56,388 --> 00:15:57,728
Hey there, Kiriyama.

414
00:15:58,168 --> 00:15:59,148
Why are you sitting there

415
00:15:59,148 --> 00:15:59,748
all alone?

416
00:16:00,008 --> 00:16:01,828
That's no good, right?

417
00:16:02,448 --> 00:16:03,488
Please don't make me

418
00:16:03,488 --> 00:16:04,668
the focus of next week's

419
00:16:04,668 --> 00:16:05,488
homeroom assignment.

420
00:16:05,488 --> 00:16:06,408
Everyone be nice

421
00:16:06,408 --> 00:16:07,108
to Kiriyama.

422
00:16:08,488 --> 00:16:09,728
What the heck?

423
00:16:10,068 --> 00:16:11,368
That would be the worst.

424
00:16:11,928 --> 00:16:12,788
It's tough enough

425
00:16:12,788 --> 00:16:14,348
just having everyone hate me.

426
00:16:14,728 --> 00:16:16,268
But to be put on display

427
00:16:16,268 --> 00:16:17,208
on top of that

428
00:16:17,208 --> 00:16:18,428
wouldn't solve anything.

429
00:16:19,108 --> 00:16:20,628
It would only bring attention

430
00:16:20,628 --> 00:16:21,208
to the fact

431
00:16:21,208 --> 00:16:22,928
that everyone despises me.

432
00:16:23,368 --> 00:16:25,028
No, I gotta avoid that

433
00:16:25,028 --> 00:16:25,888
no matter what.

434
00:16:28,308 --> 00:16:28,828
There.

435
00:16:29,088 --> 00:16:30,068
It's kind of far,

436
00:16:30,208 --> 00:16:31,308
but I'll go over there.

437
00:16:35,488 --> 00:16:37,168
It'll be okay.

438
00:16:37,508 --> 00:16:38,288
This'll work.

439
00:16:39,248 --> 00:16:41,008
I'll just quietly walk

440
00:16:41,008 --> 00:16:41,988
and not run.

441
00:16:42,448 --> 00:16:43,848
If I just walk normally,

442
00:16:44,208 --> 00:16:45,588
then I won't stand out.

443
00:16:46,888 --> 00:16:47,528
Slowly,

444
00:16:47,948 --> 00:16:48,488
normally...

445
00:16:48,488 --> 00:16:54,388
I did it!

446
00:16:54,748 --> 00:16:55,548
I made it!

447
00:16:59,788 --> 00:17:00,728
It's cold

448
00:17:00,728 --> 00:17:01,528
and damp.

449
00:17:02,448 --> 00:17:03,308
I know.

450
00:17:03,608 --> 00:17:04,288
I'll just use

451
00:17:04,288 --> 00:17:05,188
one of my folders.

452
00:17:05,188 --> 00:17:19,648
There are a bunch of ants.

453
00:17:20,428 --> 00:17:21,028
Please,

454
00:17:21,148 --> 00:17:22,368
don't crawl on my lunch.

455
00:17:23,528 --> 00:17:24,468
I know.

456
00:17:24,468 --> 00:17:32,428
There you go.

457
00:17:33,628 --> 00:17:34,888
I wonder if ants

458
00:17:34,888 --> 00:17:35,648
can even carry

459
00:17:35,648 --> 00:17:37,068
a piece of candy that big.

460
00:17:38,208 --> 00:17:39,348
I guess they have to

461
00:17:39,348 --> 00:17:39,988
break it up

462
00:17:39,988 --> 00:17:41,268
into tiny little pieces.

463
00:17:42,828 --> 00:17:44,568
Sounds like a lot of work.

464
00:17:44,568 --> 00:17:44,888
Huh?

465
00:17:54,468 --> 00:17:56,068
I made a copy of this

466
00:17:56,068 --> 00:17:57,068
from Father's book,

467
00:17:57,548 --> 00:18:00,068
Checkmate in 117 Moves.

468
00:18:01,668 --> 00:18:03,208
Oh, you solved it?

469
00:18:03,388 --> 00:18:04,688
The one with 85 moves?

470
00:18:05,188 --> 00:18:06,128
Incredible, Ray.

471
00:18:06,628 --> 00:18:07,688
I couldn't figure out

472
00:18:07,688 --> 00:18:08,588
how to solve that one

473
00:18:08,588 --> 00:18:09,948
until I was in middle school.

474
00:18:10,748 --> 00:18:11,788
My adopted father

475
00:18:11,788 --> 00:18:13,308
is a professional shogi player.

476
00:18:14,408 --> 00:18:15,108
He went pro

477
00:18:15,108 --> 00:18:15,968
when he was 19.

478
00:18:17,608 --> 00:18:19,248
I wonder if my father

479
00:18:19,248 --> 00:18:20,488
will be happy with me

480
00:18:20,488 --> 00:18:22,828
if I can solve

481
00:18:22,828 --> 00:18:23,988
this problem, too.

482
00:18:24,468 --> 00:18:32,648
All right, everyone.

483
00:18:32,868 --> 00:18:33,448
Time to go.

484
00:18:33,888 --> 00:18:34,148
Huh?

485
00:18:34,388 --> 00:18:35,668
Um, is it 1.30?

486
00:18:35,888 --> 00:18:37,268
I gotta clean everything up.

487
00:18:37,608 --> 00:18:38,488
I hope I didn't leave

488
00:18:38,488 --> 00:18:39,168
anything else

489
00:18:39,168 --> 00:18:40,048
lying around here.

490
00:18:40,528 --> 00:18:42,028
Oh, the ants.

491
00:18:42,248 --> 00:18:44,008
They ate so much already.

492
00:18:44,868 --> 00:18:45,428
Amazing!

493
00:18:46,268 --> 00:18:47,588
I had no idea.

494
00:18:48,388 --> 00:18:49,568
Even though the ants

495
00:18:49,568 --> 00:18:50,388
are so tiny,

496
00:18:50,728 --> 00:18:51,588
they melted away

497
00:18:51,588 --> 00:18:53,228
the candy super fast.

498
00:18:53,228 --> 00:18:55,388
Let's go, Kiriyama.

499
00:18:55,708 --> 00:18:56,328
You're late.

500
00:18:56,428 --> 00:18:57,408
Where were you, huh?

501
00:18:58,168 --> 00:18:58,648
Sorry.

502
00:18:59,568 --> 00:19:01,128
The bathroom was crowded,

503
00:19:01,408 --> 00:19:02,228
so...

504
00:19:02,228 --> 00:19:04,408
It's time for us to go.

505
00:19:04,768 --> 00:19:06,008
Is everyone's seat neighbor

506
00:19:06,008 --> 00:19:06,648
here now?

507
00:19:06,648 --> 00:19:07,148
Yeah!

508
00:19:09,288 --> 00:19:11,368
Wait, where's yours, Kiriyama?

509
00:19:11,748 --> 00:19:13,288
Uh, no one was sitting here, sir,

510
00:19:13,388 --> 00:19:14,108
so it's okay.

511
00:19:14,108 --> 00:19:16,708
Oh, that's right.

512
00:19:16,708 --> 00:19:18,548
Well, since everyone's here,

513
00:19:18,768 --> 00:19:19,608
let's go!

514
00:19:19,788 --> 00:19:20,288
Okay!

515
00:19:22,288 --> 00:19:23,428
When I said no one

516
00:19:23,428 --> 00:19:24,268
was sitting here,

517
00:19:24,648 --> 00:19:26,128
I could feel a big lump

518
00:19:26,128 --> 00:19:27,468
in the back of my throat.

519
00:19:29,148 --> 00:19:30,168
I wonder

520
00:19:30,168 --> 00:19:32,188
if the seat next to me

521
00:19:32,188 --> 00:19:33,488
will always be empty

522
00:19:33,488 --> 00:19:35,508
for the rest of my life.

523
00:19:35,508 --> 00:19:41,128
All right.

524
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:42,408
Next seat five.

525
00:19:42,728 --> 00:19:43,468
Have a good game.

526
00:19:45,028 --> 00:19:45,928
For me,

527
00:19:46,148 --> 00:19:47,188
that was it.

528
00:19:47,568 --> 00:19:48,808
It was the magic ticket.

529
00:19:49,968 --> 00:19:50,968
Good luck.

530
00:19:52,108 --> 00:19:53,988
As long as I had that ticket,

531
00:19:54,988 --> 00:19:57,048
somebody would always

532
00:19:57,048 --> 00:20:00,368
automatically

533
00:20:00,368 --> 00:20:03,668
sit right across from me.

534
00:20:03,668 --> 00:20:09,128
I encountered

535
00:20:09,128 --> 00:20:10,668
many different kinds of people.

536
00:20:12,868 --> 00:20:13,428
Crap!

537
00:20:13,528 --> 00:20:14,988
Who is this little brat?

538
00:20:15,208 --> 00:20:16,368
You're too good.

539
00:20:16,848 --> 00:20:17,208
Hmm.

540
00:20:17,888 --> 00:20:18,608
Damn it.

541
00:20:18,908 --> 00:20:20,068
I'll walk you to the station

542
00:20:20,068 --> 00:20:21,388
since it's already dark.

543
00:20:21,568 --> 00:20:22,548
Here, drink this.

544
00:20:23,028 --> 00:20:23,908
Do you like cocoa?

545
00:20:24,248 --> 00:20:24,788
Or what?

546
00:20:25,128 --> 00:20:26,048
Uh, yes, sir.

547
00:20:26,148 --> 00:20:26,748
Thank you.

548
00:20:27,268 --> 00:20:29,008
Some acted like they were nice.

549
00:20:30,268 --> 00:20:31,948
And of course...

550
00:20:31,948 --> 00:20:33,608
Wow, you're pretty weak.

551
00:20:34,088 --> 00:20:34,988
I wonder why Kota

552
00:20:34,988 --> 00:20:35,988
would take you in

553
00:20:35,988 --> 00:20:36,788
as his apprentice.

554
00:20:37,988 --> 00:20:39,548
Some didn't like me at all.

555
00:20:41,708 --> 00:20:44,308
But as long as I kept fighting,

556
00:20:45,028 --> 00:20:46,188
someone would always

557
00:20:46,188 --> 00:20:47,528
end up sitting in front of me.

558
00:20:49,608 --> 00:20:50,848
This is the ticket.

559
00:20:51,508 --> 00:20:53,188
As long as I have this,

560
00:20:54,068 --> 00:20:56,328
I know I belong somewhere.

561
00:20:56,328 --> 00:21:02,068
This ticket is my lifeline.

562
00:21:04,068 --> 00:21:05,828
I don't have to go anywhere.

563
00:21:06,928 --> 00:21:08,788
I can just keep on riding.

564
00:21:09,788 --> 00:21:11,448
And that's fine with me.

565
00:21:13,028 --> 00:21:14,568
If I get off this train,

566
00:21:14,868 --> 00:21:16,008
I'll have nowhere to go.

567
00:21:16,008 --> 00:21:20,328
This ticket alone

568
00:21:20,328 --> 00:21:22,008
could take me all the way

569
00:21:22,008 --> 00:21:22,608
to tomorrow.

570
00:21:23,728 --> 00:21:25,508
So I have to hold on tight.

571
00:21:25,868 --> 00:21:27,568
Like my life depends on it.

572
00:21:28,768 --> 00:21:30,448
I have to protect it.

573
00:21:32,388 --> 00:21:33,828
At all costs.

574
00:21:33,828 --> 00:21:42,188
Hey, Kiriyama!

575
00:21:43,188 --> 00:21:43,628
Kiriyama!

576
00:21:44,288 --> 00:21:47,728
What are you spacing out about?

577
00:21:47,888 --> 00:21:48,948
Come on, sit down.

578
00:21:49,248 --> 00:21:50,268
He just made a move

579
00:21:50,268 --> 00:21:51,228
and it was amazing.

580
00:21:52,368 --> 00:21:52,728
Whoa.

581
00:21:53,748 --> 00:21:55,608
Sacrificing the 5-3 pawn plus

582
00:21:55,608 --> 00:21:56,548
was a great move.

583
00:21:56,928 --> 00:21:58,048
With gold to same

584
00:21:58,048 --> 00:21:59,108
and rook to 7-7,

585
00:21:59,288 --> 00:21:59,828
what do you think

586
00:21:59,828 --> 00:22:00,748
is next, Kiriyama?

587
00:22:01,568 --> 00:22:02,908
How much time is left?

588
00:22:03,308 --> 00:22:04,988
Mr. Fujimoto has 8 minutes

589
00:22:04,988 --> 00:22:06,268
and Mr. Shimada

590
00:22:06,268 --> 00:22:07,108
has less than 3.

591
00:22:07,668 --> 00:22:08,468
First of all,

592
00:22:08,708 --> 00:22:10,028
crush the rook at 7-7.

593
00:22:10,768 --> 00:22:12,148
Then you take the initiative

594
00:22:12,148 --> 00:22:13,728
by moving gold to 6-4.

595
00:22:14,008 --> 00:22:15,008
Gold to 6-4?

596
00:22:15,168 --> 00:22:16,488
Not the pawn at 7-3?

597
00:22:16,668 --> 00:22:17,468
If you do that,

598
00:22:17,568 --> 00:22:18,168
it'll be tough

599
00:22:18,168 --> 00:22:19,548
against the bishop to 6-2.

600
00:22:20,428 --> 00:22:22,168
It's not like I've changed, really.

601
00:22:23,948 --> 00:22:25,048
And also...

602
00:22:28,048 --> 00:22:29,828
the people around me

603
00:22:29,828 --> 00:22:30,748
haven't changed, either.

604
00:22:39,208 --> 00:22:40,408
It's just that,

605
00:22:40,908 --> 00:22:42,088
while desperately playing

606
00:22:42,088 --> 00:22:43,388
the game over and over.

607
00:22:44,168 --> 00:22:45,268
Every single day,

608
00:22:45,748 --> 00:22:46,348
it seemed like

609
00:22:46,348 --> 00:22:47,248
my head would spin.

610
00:22:51,508 --> 00:22:52,368
One day,

611
00:22:52,568 --> 00:22:53,308
I realized

612
00:22:53,308 --> 00:22:54,708
that other people

613
00:22:54,708 --> 00:22:55,708
were traveling with me

614
00:22:55,708 --> 00:22:56,368
on that train.

615
00:22:58,048 --> 00:22:59,348
All moving toward

616
00:22:59,348 --> 00:23:00,408
the shining light.

